# The line that sets up this machine and every Super Banana project in the current folder, on
# Windows:
#
#   irm https://super-banana-studios.github.io/setup-win | iex
#
# `irm ... | iex` cannot pass arguments to what it runs - the script arrives as text and nothing
# else - so the repository whose tools/setup.sh does the work is named here. That script takes
# the folder the window stands in as the projects folder. super-banana.cmd next to this file runs
# the same line from the folder it lies in, with a double click.
#
# No `exit` anywhere: this runs inside the person's own PowerShell window, and `exit` closes that
# window rather than this script (measured on 5.1.26100.9444).
& ([scriptblock]::Create((irm https://super-banana-studios.github.io/setup.ps1))) -Repo Super-Banana-Studios/setup
